  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Environmental Education outreach to</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The primary objective of the project, Environmental Education Outreach to Schools &#x2013; Tiwai Island Communities- Phase II is to motivate all of the pupils and teachers from the 6 schools to participate actively in initiating, planning and implementing programmes for the restoration of their local environment and deepen their respect  for and understanding of their natural heritage. The key project outcomes are:
&#x2022; Increased collection and nursing of indigenous trees from local forests, thus the tree cover around the schools is expected to grow significantly.
&#x2022; Increased awareness among the children and communities, about the benefit of land restoration, protection of forests and conservation of biodiversity and environmental issues.
&#x2022; Increased awareness and understanding of environmental issues in targeted schools and communities.</narrative>
  </description>
